completed_at: "2026-10-21T18:53:45.721Z"
author: codex-agent
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: A real shallow-merge regression covers bad/run/status when the first bad commit has an omitted parent; available explicit associations remain available; missing provenance has an honest omission or boundary receipt; complete-history and root-commit reports remain correct.
parent: pm-vcs-p7bisect
repro_steps: "Create an empty-tree ancestor A, good G with parent A, side S with parent A, and merge M with parents G and S. Clone M with depth 2 so A is absent and G/S are shallow. Initialize a real tracker and linked test in the clone. Start bisect G M, mark S bad, then request status."
resolution: Delivered by the audit-linked mainline implementation.
expected_result: Preserve bisect reports when the culprit is a shallow boundary.
actual_result: "Re-verified unchanged main 27e1d84671fa: delivery 3fb4ecd29e10, 27e1d84671fa remains in main ancestry; engine/annotate.ts, test/attribution.test.ts remain present."
