comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-19T23:25:30.095Z",codex-agent,"Fixed in PR 131 review round: real depth-two merge clone verifies missing ancestor, manual bad plus status, automatic run plus status, explicit association deduplication/order, honest itemsBoundary=shallow, no hydration, restored HEAD and reset. Focused regression passes; reverting only linkedItems fails on missing parent. Related traceFile shallow-parent read fixed with an independent passing/reverting regression. Item remains in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-20T00:22:31.544Z",codex-agent,"Final acceptance: linked command node --test --test-name-pattern=\"shallow culprit\" test/bisect.test.ts passed 1/1 via pinned PM. Both full release gates passed 1709/1709 with all 70 production files at unchanged per-file 100 percent coverage in all dimensions. The regression covers manual bad and automated run followed by status, retains sorted explicit links, reports itemsBoundary=shallow, preserves missing ancestry and original HEAD, and resets successfully. Reverting only linkedItems independently fails on the omitted parent. Releasing the claim; item remains in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-21T18:53:23.868Z",codex-agent,"Tracker reconciliation authorized for the audited verdict FIXED-STALE. Re-verified unchanged main 27e1d84671fa: delivery 3fb4ecd29e10, 27e1d84671fa remains in main ancestry; engine/annotate.ts, test/attribution.test.ts remain present. Preserve bisect reports when the culprit is a shallow boundary. PRs #131/#136 (3fb4ecd/27e1d84) deliver linked-test bisect and shallow-boundary report preservation with explicit omission receipts. Scope: tracker state only; no new runtime certification or deployment claim."
